Subject: [PATCH] webrtc: gather the given address when UDP cannot be used

Behind a proxy that carries no datagrams, or under the
disable_non_proxied_udp policy, WebRTC creates no UDP socket and a page
gets no UDP candidate. --fingerprint-webrtc-ip only rewrote candidates
that exist, so it did nothing there: a page saw a public address over
HTTP and none in WebRTC, which Pixelscan reports as a WebRTC leak.

With the switch set and UDP unusable, the allocation sequence of the
switch's address family gathers over a socket that never sends. It
answers a binding request to a configured STUN server with the given
address, as that server would, and drops every other datagram. WebRTC
then builds the candidates of a host with that public address itself:
foundations, priorities and ports as usual, an mDNS name for a host
candidate, and only the candidates the IP handling policy allows. No
packet, and no DNS query for a STUN server, leaves the machine, and no
local address appears. Connectivity checks still fail, as they do
without UDP, and TURN over TCP and TLS works as before. Without the
switch nothing changes.

The candidate text rewrite of patch 0073 now keeps an mDNS name and an
empty related address, as stock Chrome shows them.

diff --git a/third_party/webrtc/api/candidate.cc b/third_party/webrtc/api/candidate.cc
index 2398b96f8a..9b0aad86fb 100644
--- a/third_party/webrtc/api/candidate.cc
+++ b/third_party/webrtc/api/candidate.cc
@@ -90,7 +90,10 @@ std::string BuildCandidate(const Candidate& candidate, bool include_ufrag) {
           : candidate.address().ipaddr().ToString();
   bool address_overridden = false;
 #if defined(WEBRTC_CHROMIUM_BUILD)
-  if (candidate.is_stun() || candidate.is_local()) {
+  // An mDNS name hides the address already, and stock Chrome shows one there,
+  // so it is kept.
+  if ((candidate.is_stun() || candidate.is_local()) &&
+      !candidate.address().ipaddr().IsNil()) {
     const base::CommandLine* command_line =
         base::CommandLine::ForCurrentProcess();
     if (command_line->HasSwitch("fingerprint-webrtc-ip")) {
@@ -113,8 +116,9 @@ std::string BuildCandidate(const Candidate& candidate, bool include_ufrag) {
   // Related address
   if (!candidate.related_address().IsNil()) {
     os << kAttributeCandidateRaddr << " "
-       << (address_overridden ? address
-                              : candidate.related_address().ipaddr().ToString())
+       << (address_overridden && !candidate.related_address().IsAnyIP()
+               ? address
+               : candidate.related_address().ipaddr().ToString())
        << " "
        << kAttributeCandidateRport << " "
        << candidate.related_address().PortAsString() << " ";
